WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.732
Development, staging, and production
environments should not share the same

2
00:00:07.812 --> 00:00:13.949
assumptions, credentials, state,
variables, or approval paths.

3
00:00:14.029 --> 00:00:19.069
IaC workflows should make these boundaries
explicit.

4
00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:26.710
Environment separation reduces the chance
that a lower-risk workflow can affect

5
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:31.392
production resources or expose production
data.

6
00:00:31.472 --> 00:00:37.061
Promotion gives teams a controlled way to
build confidence.

7
00:00:37.141 --> 00:00:42.839
A change can be tested in a lower-risk
environment, reviewed,

8
00:00:42.919 --> 00:00:49.603
and then promoted to production through a
path that preserves evidence.

9
00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:56.477
Teams should know what changed, who
reviewed it, which plan was approved,

10
00:00:56.557 --> 00:01:04.228
which artifact or commit was promoted, and
which environment received the update.

11
00:01:04.308 --> 00:01:10.444
High-impact changes may require approval
gates, change windows,

12
00:01:10.524 --> 00:01:15.127
stakeholder coordination, staged
application,

13
00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:21.562
or canary-style rollout where the platform
and workflow support it.

14
00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:26.464
The goal is controlled confidence, not
blind speed.

15
00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:30.488
Some changes are safe to apply frequently.

16
00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:37.472
Others affect foundational networking,
identity, encryption, storage,

17
00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:42.812
or production availability and deserve
stronger gates.

18
00:01:42.892 --> 00:01:48.590
The workflow should prevent accidental
production applies.

19
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:55.683
That means explicit target selection,
protected production credentials,

20
00:01:55.763 --> 00:02:00.803
separate state backends, protected
branches or tags,

21
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:04.061
and clear approval requirements.

22
00:02:04.141 --> 00:02:10.168
If a script or pipeline cannot confirm the
intended environment,

23
00:02:10.248 --> 00:02:14.193
it should fail before it changes anything.

24
00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:21.943
Controlled promotion turns infrastructure
change into a reviewable operational

25
00:02:22.023 --> 00:02:22.900
process.
